cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kipi in your work, please cite it."
title: kipi
abstract: >-
  kipi is an open-source, self-hosted OSINT investigation platform. It turns
  documents (PDFs, screenshots, spreadsheets, notes) into a live, typed entity
  graph, then runs an autonomous investigator agent that digs the open web,
  pivots on infrastructure, grades findings by evidence tier, and writes a
  brief. Includes graph analytics (centrality, communities, pathfinding) and a
  keyless-first OSINT tool belt.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kipnis
    given-names: Assaf
repository-code: "https://github.com/assafkip/kipi"
url: "https://github.com/assafkip/kipi"
license: Elastic-2.0
keywords:
  - osint
  - threat-intelligence
  - entity-graph
  - graph-analytics
  - link-analysis
  - fraud-investigation
  - intelligence-analysis
  - self-hosted
